API.md §4 Finding.Layer, F11, EVALUATION.md §9.3 step 3 (orchestrator ruling EVAL-AMENDNOTE round 6): a re-derived default's layer is the last amendment that changed a field it reads; a later amendment of a field it does not read keeps that layer, so the order of a layer's lines changes nothing: url, outside its refinement once port is amended, is set by layer one whether port's line comes before name's (first) or after (second).
-- layers --
one
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Server.
record Server {
  /// Port.
  port: Int = 1
  /// Name.
  name: String = "n"
  /// URL.
  url: String(..=6) = "h:{port}"
}

/// Port first.
let first: Server = {}

/// Name first.
let second: Server = {}
-- a/one.canon --
package a
layer one

amend first {
  port: 90000
  name: "x"
}

amend second {
  name: "x"
  port: 90001
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3204]  a/a.canon:11:23
  first.url: h:90000 is outside ..=6
  set by layer one
  expected by a/a.canon:11 (url: String(..=6))

error[E3204]  a/a.canon:11:23
  second.url: h:90001 is outside ..=6
  set by layer one
  expected by a/a.canon:11 (url: String(..=6))

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
